--- Draws text at `x, y`. Call it inside `draw()` to show the text every frame.
--- Set [`style.fontSize()`](style.json#style.fontSize), [`style.font()`](style.json#style.font), and [`style.fill()`](style.json#style.fill)
--- before drawing to choose its size, font, and color. Emoji work by default.
--- 
--- Use `\n` for a new line, or supply `w` to wrap a longer message. Add `h`
--- to align the text within a box using [`style.textAlign()`](style.json#style.textAlign). The box controls
--- layout; it does not clip text that extends beyond it. Numbers and other values
--- are converted to strings.
--- 
--- See [Drawing](../manual/drawing.json) for positioning, wrapping, shadows, and tagged-text
--- examples. For advanced per-letter effects, see `text.style`.
---@param str any The value to draw (converted to a string).
---@param x number The x coordinate of the text.
---@param y number The y coordinate of the text.
---@param w? number Optional wrapping width in points; zero means unbounded.
---@param h? number Optional box height in points; zero means unbounded.
function text(str, x, y, w, h) end

