--- Returns the arc tangent of y/x (in radians), using the signs of both arguments to find the quadrant of the result. It also handles correctly the case of x being zero
--- 
--- The default value for x is 1, so that the call math.atan(y) returns the arc tangent of y
---@param y number numerator for arc tangent
---@param x number denominator for arc tangent (defaults to 1)
---@return any
function math.atan(y, x) end

--- This function returns the smallest integer larger than or equal to value. This rounds a number up to the nearest integer. For example, math.ceil(5.2) returns 6.
---@param value any int or float, compute the smallest integer larger than or equal to this number
---@return integer
function math.ceil(value) end

--- This function returns the cosine of value (assumed to be in radians).
---@param value any int or float, compute the cosine of this number
---@return any
function math.cos(value) end

--- This function returns hyperbolic cosine of value.
---@param value any int or float, compute the hyperbolic cosine of this number
---@return any
function math.cosh(value) end

--- This function returns the angle specified by value (given in radians) in degrees.
---@param value any int or float, angle in radians to convert to degrees
---@return any
